{"excerpt_id":"ex_b9c427878132_005","source_id":"src_b9c427878132","source_hash":"38c9afb58132d7109c0b29f070699c502f9071b8e4558ec1685bd387fff0e54e","text":"Title: Yrast band in the heavy $N = Z$ nucleus $^{88}$Ru: $α$-cluster approach","location_hint":"paragraph 18","char_start":816,"char_end":894,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T18:37:26.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_b9c427878132_006","source_id":"src_b9c427878132","source_hash":"38c9afb58132d7109c0b29f070699c502f9071b8e4558ec1685bd387fff0e54e","text":"View a PDF of the paper titled Yrast band in the heavy $N = Z$ nucleus $^{88}$Ru: $\\alpha$-cluster approach, by Peter Mohr","location_hint":"paragraph 20","char_start":921,"char_end":1043,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T18:37:26.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_b9c427878132_007","source_id":"src_b9c427878132","source_hash":"38c9afb58132d7109c0b29f070699c502f9071b8e4558ec1685bd387fff0e54e","text":"Abstract: The yrast band in the heavy $N = Z$ nucleus $^{88}$Ru is studied in the framework of the $\\alpha$-cluster model in combination with double-folding potentials.","location_hint":"paragraph 22","char_start":1057,"char_end":1225,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T18:37:26.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_b9c427878132_008","source_id":"src_b9c427878132","source_hash":"38c9afb58132d7109c0b29f070699c502f9071b8e4558ec1685bd387fff0e54e","text":"It is found that the excitation energies of the yrast band in $^{88}$Ru can be nicely described within the $\\alpha$-cluster approach using a smooth and mildly $L$-dependent adjustment of the potential strength.","location_hint":"paragraph 22","char_start":1226,"char_end":1436,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T18:37:26.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_b9c427878132_009","source_id":"src_b9c427878132","source_hash":"38c9afb58132d7109c0b29f070699c502f9071b8e4558ec1685bd387fff0e54e","text":"This result is similar to well-established $\\alpha$-cluster states in nuclei with a (magic core $\\otimes$ $\\alpha$) structure.","location_hint":"paragraph 22","char_start":1437,"char_end":1563,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T18:37:26.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_b9c427878132_010","source_id":"src_b9c427878132","source_hash":"38c9afb58132d7109c0b29f070699c502f9071b8e4558ec1685bd387fff0e54e","text":"Contrary, the yrast bands in neighboring $N \\ne Z$ nuclei deviate from such a typical $\\alpha$-cluster behavior.","location_hint":"paragraph 22","char_start":1564,"char_end":1676,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T18:37:26.150Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_b9c427878132_011","source_id":"src_b9c427878132","source_hash":"38c9afb58132d7109c0b29f070699c502f9071b8e4558ec1685bd387fff0e54e","text":"Finally, the $\\alpha$-cluster model predicts reduced transition strengths of about 10 Weisskopf units for intraband transitions between low-lying states in the yrast band of $^{88}$Ru.","location_hint":"paragraph 22","char_start":1677,"char_end":1861,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T18:37:26.150Z"}
